      "type": "architecture",
      "title": "Keyed Kafka event flow and ownership",
      "description": "A synthetic order producer sends keyed records to a partitioned Kafka topic. A consumer group owns processing, commits progress after completed work, writes a duplicate-safe search outcome, and diverts failures to a retained retry topic with a human replay owner.",
